## PortaleZilioService - Daily Summary (2026-03-10)

- Fixed model setup in `PortaleZilioService` to avoid duplicate-table conflicts with `MonitoraggioImpianti`.
- Stabilized `home.html` structure with grouped panels and partial tables.
- Added and aligned table partials with current `view_models.py` fields.
- Introduced grouped headers (`O&M Ordinaria` / `Straordinario`) and visual separators.
- Added/ordered confirmed columns, including `Mancata Produzione` and `Totale Annuo su MW`.
- Created `FvMetadata` model + migrations for FV business metadata not available in legacy tables.
- Added admin management for `FvMetadata` with ordered fields for manual data entry.
- Switched `rows_builder.py` to read FV rows from `FvMetadata` (category/flags/contracts), with placeholders for not-yet-implemented metrics.
- Resolved runtime errors encountered during setup:
  - duplicate `db_table` mapping
  - bad imports / stale file state
  - SQLite lock during migration
  - invalid field access (e.g., `nome_cliente` on wrong model)
  - wrong queryset filters (e.g., `tipo` on `FvMetadata`)

## Current Status

- `FvMetadata` table exists and can be populated from Django admin.
- UI table columns are aligned with the confirmed structure.
- Basic row population works; many computed/API fields still intentionally set to `--`.

## Overview Tables Logic

The FV tables shown in `PortaleZilioService/overview.html` are currently built in:

- `Produzione/PortaleZilioService/services/rows_builder_portale.py`

The table assignment logic is based on these fields:

- `ImpiantoAnagrafica.tipo_impianto`
- `ImpiantoAnagrafica.stato_impianto`
- `FotovoltaicoMetadata.categoria_fv`
- `FotovoltaicoMetadata.is_oem`
- `FotovoltaicoMetadata.is_ppu`
- `FotovoltaicoMetadata.is_agrivoltaico`

Important rule:

- if a FV plant is `IN_COSTRUZIONE`, it must appear only in the `FV In Costruzione` table
- it must be excluded from all the other FV tables

### FV Table Matrix

| Table | tipo_impianto | stato_impianto | categoria_fv | is_oem | is_ppu | is_agrivoltaico | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| FV In Costruzione | `FOTOVOLTAICO` | `IN_COSTRUZIONE` | any | any | any | any | dominant rule: if a plant is in construction, it goes only here |
| O&M FV Clienti | `FOTOVOLTAICO` | `!= IN_COSTRUZIONE` | `CLIENTE` | `True` | any | any | can coexist with `PPU FV` and `O&M Agrivoltaico` |
| O&M FV Proprieta | `FOTOVOLTAICO` | `!= IN_COSTRUZIONE` | `PROPRIETA` | `True` | any | any | can coexist with `PPU FV` and `O&M Agrivoltaico` |
| O&M Agrivoltaico | `FOTOVOLTAICO` | `!= IN_COSTRUZIONE` | any | `True` | any | `True` | can coexist with `Clienti`, `Proprieta`, `PPU` |
| PPU FV | `FOTOVOLTAICO` | `!= IN_COSTRUZIONE` | any | any | `True` | any | can coexist with O&M and Agrivoltaico |

### Practical Consequences

- `CLIENTE + is_oem=True` -> `O&M FV Clienti`
- `CLIENTE + is_oem=True + is_ppu=True` -> `O&M FV Clienti` + `PPU FV`
- `PROPRIETA + is_oem=True + is_agrivoltaico=True` -> `O&M FV Proprieta` + `O&M Agrivoltaico`
- `PROPRIETA + is_oem=True + is_ppu=True + is_agrivoltaico=True` -> `O&M FV Proprieta` + `O&M Agrivoltaico` + `PPU FV`
- any FV plant with `stato_impianto = IN_COSTRUZIONE` -> only `FV In Costruzione`

## How To Configure A New FV Plant

When inserting or updating a new FV plant, keep these rules in mind.

### 1. Set the business category correctly

`categoria_fv` is exclusive and must represent the plant business category:

- `CLIENTE`
- `PROPRIETA`

Do not duplicate this logic with extra booleans such as `is_cliente` or `is_di_proprieta`.

### 2. Mark the transversal flags independently

Use these flags to decide in which additional tables the plant can appear:

- `is_oem=True` if the plant must appear in one of the O&M tables
- `is_ppu=True` if the plant must also appear in `PPU FV`
- `is_agrivoltaico=True` if the plant must also appear in `O&M Agrivoltaico`

These flags are independent and can coexist.

### 3. Treat `IN_COSTRUZIONE` as dominant

If the plant is still under construction:

- set `stato_impianto = IN_COSTRUZIONE`
- the plant must appear only in `FV In Costruzione`
- it must not appear in `O&M FV Clienti`
- it must not appear in `O&M FV Proprieta`
- it must not appear in `O&M Agrivoltaico`
- it must not appear in `PPU FV`

### 4. Make sure `FotovoltaicoMetadata` exists

The tables `O&M FV Clienti`, `O&M FV Proprieta`, `O&M Agrivoltaico`, and `PPU FV` rely on `FotovoltaicoMetadata`.

If the metadata record is missing, the plant will not appear in those tables even if the anagrafica exists.

### 5. Use coherent combinations

Recommended examples:

- client O&M plant:
  - `categoria_fv = CLIENTE`
  - `is_oem = True`
  - `is_ppu = False`
  - `is_agrivoltaico = False`

- proprietary O&M agrivoltaic plant:
  - `categoria_fv = PROPRIETA`
  - `is_oem = True`
  - `is_agrivoltaico = True`

- client PPU + O&M plant:
  - `categoria_fv = CLIENTE`
  - `is_oem = True`
  - `is_ppu = True`

- plant under construction:
  - `stato_impianto = IN_COSTRUZIONE`
  - other flags may remain set, but table visibility is overridden by the construction state

### 6. Verify expected visibility after insert/update

After saving a new plant, check whether it appears in the expected table set:

- only `FV In Costruzione` if it is in construction
- one or more O&M / PPU / Agrivoltaico tables if it is not in construction

This is especially important for plants that should intentionally appear in more than one table.

